# `app_state` lock — UI deadlock

Canonical: `docs/DEV.md` bug **7a**.

## Fact (gdb, Khaynjo 2026-11-03)

Hung process: main thread on `futex_do_wait` / `Mutex::lock` of `app_state::STATE` inside `set_status_line_only` ← `set_status` ← Settings Bill/place tap.

Not wrap/Fill spam (that is bug 7; different signature: draw-time / high log volume).

## Forbidden

```rust
self.set_status(cx, app_state().lock().unwrap().t("…"));
self.set_status(cx, app_state().lock().unwrap().t("…").replace(…));
```

The temporary `MutexGuard` lives for the whole statement. `set_status` locks again → same-thread deadlock → OS “Not Responding”.

## Required

```rust
self.set_status(cx, app_t("…"));
// or
let msg = { let st = app_state().lock().unwrap(); st.t("…").replace(…) };
self.set_status(cx, msg);
```

`app_t` is in each app’s `runtime.rs`. Duplicate the same fix per app — no shared core.

Before claiming a Settings hang is wrap/Fill: dump stacks (`futex` + `app_state::STATE` vs turtle/draw).
